# build output
bin/

# test binaries (anchored to repo root — unanchored "agent"/"gopi"
# accidentally ignored cmd/agent/* and internal/agent/*)
/agent
/gopi
.gopi-tags
# The ctags index's IN-FLIGHT temp (internal/tools/symbol.go:62 `tagsIndexTempPrefix`
# = `.gopi-tags-tmp-` + `*`, from tagsIndexFileName + "-tmp-"). ctags writes it into
# the index's OWN directory and renames it into place, so a rebuild inside `cmd/agent`
# materialises `cmd/agent/.gopi-tags-tmp-<random>` for its lifetime. The line above
# matches that NAME EXACTLY and therefore misses the temp: measured 2026-10-31
# (`git check-ignore -v cmd/agent/.gopi-tags-tmp-2642549001` ⇒ exit 1, NOT ignored),
# and `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` then reported it as an untracked
# file — which TestSyncBarePeersTestCoversEveryChangedFile read as "this run created
# it" and reded on, in a tree where nothing was ever changed. Any test that reaches
# code_search from cmd/agent makes it appear at a random instant, which is exactly
# why that ratchet looked nondeterministic.
.gopi-tags-tmp-*

# Root-level build outputs from an EXPLICIT `-o`. A tracked recipe builds one
# here: tasks/01a0cea0-rule31-two-states.sh:35 is
# `CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o gopi-behind ./cmd/agent/`, and the A/B compare runs
# in devdoc/ build ./gopi-before / ./gopi-fixed the same way — all at the
# checkout root, and before this rule none of them was ignored
# (`git check-ignore -v gopi-behind` exited 1).
#
# The shape is a ROOT-ANCHORED PREFIX and the anchoring is the whole point. The
# accident recorded directly above was an UNANCHORED `agent`/`gopi`, which
# matched cmd/agent/* and internal/agent/* — a bare name matches at every depth.
# A leading `/` matches only the checkout root, so `/gopi-*` cannot reach into
# any directory, and `gopi-` is not even a prefix of `agent`; both classes are
# untouched by construction. `/gopi` stays on its own line because `*` requires
# at least the hyphen. A -o artifact additionally belongs in bin/ (the declared
# build home, ignored above) or the pinned scratch root — this rule only stops a
# stray one from appearing as `??` in `git status`, one `git add` from the
# commit that put `agent` in the index in the first place.
/gopi-*

