__pycache__/
.e2e/

# --- tracked-scratch hygiene (see devdoc/repo-hygiene-tracked-scratch.md) ---
# Guarded by internal/standards TestRepoRootHasNoTrackedJunk.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: any pattern for a repo-relative `scratch/` at the checkout
# root. That class IS refused by the gate above (index half), but there is no
# ignore line for it and none may be added: an ignore rule hides the writer
# instead of stopping it, and `scratch/` must stay VISIBLE as a `??` entry — it
# is the diagnosing half Rule 30 reads (`completed-unclean`), and how the 135 MB
# residue of 2026-09-26 was attributed in the first place. Ignoring it would have
# silenced the only signal that found it. History and ruling:
# devdoc/scratch-repo-residue-01a0db54.md.
#
# Go test / probe binaries: `go test -c` wrote .leakprobe-agent.test (19 MB)
# into the repo root once and it got committed. Never track a compiled test
# binary — keep `go test -o <scratch dir>` (testutil.SuiteTempRoot()) instead.
*.test

